Nice and helpful.

But one major comment...
It is not extensible as a free source would be; make the source free - that
is: publish the Word/OpenOffice/whatever docs, if you like it to be spread.
Otherwise someone interested will write an own sheet that meets exactly her
needs. See, your sheet is just two pages and no magic...

I'd prefer an on-screen version, adding the NH data to the sheet in a second
window. (No pencil no rubber, and keeping the hands on the keyboard :-)
Some form with predefined selections or a simple text document to add text.

The total number of moves could be added to the sheet.

What is the DYWYPI meant for? Apparently it is too small to take all your
possenssions. In an on-screen version you would simply copy/paste the data
to the sheet, including level snapshots to log interesting situations.

An extension to the sheet could be to list each dungeon level on the sheet
(actually just a number from 1 to 50 and some branches) and note all data
for a dungeon level on the line for the respective level.

